diff --git a/scripts/sacm_x/README.md b/scripts/sacm_x/README.md
index cf3eee2..5f02937 100644
--- a/scripts/sacm_x/README.md
+++ b/scripts/sacm_x/README.md
@@ -1,182 +1,129 @@
-# SACM-X run layout
+# Unified runs: baselines and SACM-X
 
-Use one run directory per experiment.  Training and evaluation are separate
-subdirectories so a 20-dataset evaluation never overwrites the training log
-or the checkpoint.  The `seed_<seed>` level is mandatory: it keeps every
-seed's checkpoint, logs, and 20-dataset tables separate.
+Every run, baseline or SACM-X, lives in exactly one directory:
 
 ```text
-results/sacm_x/<run>/seed_<seed>/
-  train/<preset>/
-    best_model.pth          # val-selection best (not necessarily the last epoch)
-    metrics_history.json    # per-epoch metrics + best_epoch
-    run_info.json           # checkpoint, best_epoch, last_epoch, selection
-    run.log
-  eval/<tag>/
-    <preset>/<DATASET>/
-      metrics.csv
-      results_summary.txt
-      head_audit.csv ...    # when audit flags are enabled
+results/runs/<method>/<variant>/seed_<seed>/
+  best_model.pth            # file checkpoints
+  best_model                # directory checkpoints (symlink)
+  checkpoint.json           # kind + native checkpoint path
+  run_info.json
+  metrics_history.json
+  train.log
+  predictions/              # baselines, when present
+  eval/
+    <DATASET>/
+      metrics.csv           # per-image metrics
+      summary.csv           # one canonical dataset row
+      results_summary.txt ...
     tables/
-      all_metrics.csv
-      macro_metrics.csv
+      all_metrics.csv       # unified schema
+      macro_metrics.csv     # unified long schema
       final_report.md
       final_report.csv
-      table_*.tex
-    run_eval.log
-    jobs_eval.csv
     run_manifest.json
+    eval.log
+    jobs.csv
 ```
 
-## Train
+- `method` = baseline id or `sacm_x`
+- `variant` = `default` for baselines, preset for SACM-X
+- `seed` is always part of the path
+
+There is no second user-facing layout.  ``results/paper`` and
+``results/sacm_x`` are not written by the current pipeline.
+
+## Baselines: train and evaluate 20 test sets
 
 ```bash
-SEED=0
-RUN_NAME=typed_800
+# Train one or more seeds through the unified registry.
+bash scripts/run_train.sh --model unet --seeds 0 1 --gpus 0,1
 
-OUTPUT_ROOT="results/sacm_x/${RUN_NAME}_seed${SEED}/train" \
-GPU=7 SEED="$SEED" RUN_NAME="$RUN_NAME" PRESET=full_typed \
-EPOCHS=400 VAL_INTERVAL=1 SKIP_TEST=true \
-TRAIN_ROOT="data/sacm_3shot_seed${SEED}" \
-bash scripts/sacm_x/run_sacm_x_quick.sh
+# Evaluate the saved best checkpoint on the 20 test sets.
+bash scripts/run_eval.sh --model unet --seeds 0 1 --gpus 0,1
 ```
 
-The single best checkpoint is:
+Each job writes (for example, seed 1):
 
 ```text
-$OUTPUT_ROOT/full_typed/best_model.pth
+results/runs/unet/default/seed_1/
 ```
 
-`run_info.json` records `best_epoch`, `last_epoch`, `selection_metric`, and the
-absolute checkpoint path.  Only the val-selection best is saved; the last
-epoch is not a separate file.
+The eval stage calls `collect_paper_metrics.py --layout canonical` and then
+`finalize_run.py`, so the checkpoint and the 20-dataset tables share one run
+root.
 
-## Evaluate all 20 test sets
+## SACM-X: train, then evaluate 20 test sets
 
 ```bash
 SEED=0
-RUN_NAME=typed_800
-RUN_ROOT="results/sacm_x/${RUN_NAME}_seed${SEED}"
-TRAIN_OUT="$RUN_ROOT/train"
-OUTPUT_ROOT="$RUN_ROOT/eval/main"
+PRESET=full_typed
+RUN_ROOT="results/runs/sacm_x/${PRESET}/seed${SEED}"
 
-TRAIN_OUT="$TRAIN_OUT" \
-GPU=7 SEED="$SEED" PRESET=full_typed \
+GPU=7 SEED="$SEED" PRESET="$PRESET" \
 TRAIN_ROOT="data/sacm_3shot_seed${SEED}" \
-OUTPUT_ROOT="$OUTPUT_ROOT" \
-EVAL_INPUT_MODE=aspect_pad \
-USE_WANDB=true EMPTY_GUARD=true \
-COMPONENT_METRICS=true AUDIT_HEADS_FULL=true \
-bash scripts/sacm_x/eval_sacm_x_20.sh
+OUTPUT_ROOT="$RUN_ROOT" EPOCHS=800 VAL_INTERVAL=1 SKIP_TEST=true \
+bash scripts/sacm_x/run_sacm_x_quick.sh
 ```
 
-No checkpoint copy is needed: the eval script uses
-`$TRAIN_OUT/$PRESET/best_model.pth` by default.  `OUTPUT_ROOT` is the eval
-root; if omitted and `TRAIN_OUT` ends in `/train`, it defaults to the sibling
-`eval/` directory.
-
-Results:
+Training promotes the best checkpoint to:
 
 ```text
-$OUTPUT_ROOT/$PRESET/<DATASET>/metrics.csv
-$OUTPUT_ROOT/tables/all_metrics.csv
-$OUTPUT_ROOT/tables/macro_metrics.csv
-$OUTPUT_ROOT/tables/final_report.md
-$OUTPUT_ROOT/jobs_eval.csv
-$OUTPUT_ROOT/run_manifest.json
-```
-
-## Evaluate a subset
-
-```bash
-SEED=0
-RUN_NAME=typed_800
-RUN_ROOT="results/sacm_x/${RUN_NAME}_seed${SEED}"
-TRAIN_OUT="$RUN_ROOT/train"
-OUTPUT_ROOT="$RUN_ROOT/eval/audit6"
-
-TRAIN_OUT="$TRAIN_OUT" \
-GPU=7 SEED="$SEED" PRESET=full_typed \
-TRAIN_ROOT="data/sacm_3shot_seed${SEED}" \
-OUTPUT_ROOT="$OUTPUT_ROOT" \
-DATASETS="CREMI TYRE WIRE LEAF TopoMortar OCTA-500" \
-AUDIT_HEADS=true COMPONENT_METRICS=true \
-AUDIT_THRESHOLDS="-2 -1 0 1 2" \
-bash scripts/sacm_x/eval_sacm_x_20.sh
+"$RUN_ROOT/best_model.pth"
 ```
 
-The launcher passes `--datasets` and `--preset` to the aggregator, so stale
-results from another dataset set cannot leak into the macro table.
+`run_info.json` records `best_epoch`, `last_epoch`, `selection`, `seed`, and
+the checkpoint kind/path.  Only the validation-selected best checkpoint is
+saved.
 
-## Explicit checkpoint
+Evaluate the saved checkpoint:
 
 ```bash
-SEED=0
-RUN_NAME=typed_800
-RUN_ROOT="results/sacm_x/${RUN_NAME}_seed${SEED}"
-TRAIN_OUT="$RUN_ROOT/train"
-OUTPUT_ROOT="$RUN_ROOT/eval/other"
-CKPT=/absolute/path/to/best_model.pth
-
-CKPT="$CKPT" TRAIN_OUT="$TRAIN_OUT" OUTPUT_ROOT="$OUTPUT_ROOT" \
-SEED="$SEED" PRESET=full_typed \
+GPU=7 SEED="$SEED" PRESET="$PRESET" \
+TRAIN_ROOT="data/sacm_3shot_seed${SEED}" \
+TRAIN_OUT="$RUN_ROOT" OUTPUT_ROOT="$RUN_ROOT/eval" \
+EVAL_INPUT_MODE=aspect_pad USE_WANDB=true EMPTY_GUARD=true \
+COMPONENT_METRICS=true AUDIT_HEADS_FULL=true \
 bash scripts/sacm_x/eval_sacm_x_20.sh
 ```
 
-`CKPT` overrides the default checkpoint path.
+Or run train + eval in one command by setting `SKIP_TEST=false`; the quick
+script trains, finalizes the checkpoint, then invokes the 20-dataset eval.
 
-## Selection variants
+Do not pass a hard-coded seed path.  Derive it from `SEED`, as above, so each
+seed writes to a different directory.
 
-Use a separate eval root for every decision rule:
+## Latest run index
 
 ```bash
-SEED=0
-RUN_NAME=typed_800
-RUN_ROOT="results/sacm_x/${RUN_NAME}_seed${SEED}"
-TRAIN_OUT="$RUN_ROOT/train"
-
-TRAIN_OUT="$TRAIN_OUT" SEED="$SEED" PRESET=full_typed \
-OUTPUT_ROOT="$RUN_ROOT/eval/quality" SELECTION=quality \
-bash scripts/sacm_x/eval_sacm_x_20.sh
-
-TRAIN_OUT="$TRAIN_OUT" SEED="$SEED" PRESET=full_typed \
-OUTPUT_ROOT="$RUN_ROOT/eval/head3" FIXED_HEAD=3 \
-bash scripts/sacm_x/eval_sacm_x_20.sh
+python scripts/pipeline/index_runs.py
+# results/runs_index.csv
 ```
 
-Do not reuse an eval root for a different selection rule: per-dataset files
-would be overwritten.
-
-## Auto-eval after training
-
-`run_sacm_x_quick.sh` defaults to `SKIP_TEST=false`, so after training it
-evaluates all datasets from the protocol and writes `tables/` under the
-training root.  With `SKIP_TEST=true` (used for the current 800-epoch run),
-run the evaluation command above separately.
+Columns: `family,method,variant,seed,status,checkpoint,best_epoch,eval_root,
+metrics_csv,macro_csv,manifest`.
 
-## Baseline runs
+## Reproducibility
 
-Baselines keep their original layout:
-
-```text
-results/paper/<method>/seed_<seed>/
-  best_model.pth
-  run_info.json
-  paper_metrics.csv
-  paper_macro.csv
-```
+Use the shell wrappers (`run_train.sh`, `run_eval.sh`,
+`run_sacm_x_quick.sh`, `eval_sacm_x_20.sh`) so `PYTHONHASHSEED`,
+`CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG`, OMP/MKL are fixed before Python starts.  Both
+pipelines configure deterministic kernels; SACM-X uses strict mode by
+default, baselines use best-effort strict mode (`--deterministic-strict true`
+enables strict).
 
-New baseline trainings also write `run_info.json` (method, seed, checkpoint,
-best_epoch); new baseline evaluations write `run_manifest.json` next to
-`paper_metrics.csv`.
+## Legacy results
 
-## One seed-aware index for both families
+Old runs under `results/paper` or `results/sacm_x` are not consumed by the
+current scripts.  To migrate one manually:
 
 ```bash
-python scripts/pipeline/index_runs.py \
-  --roots results/paper results/sacm_x \
-  --out results/runs_index.csv
+python scripts/pipeline/finalize_run.py \
+  --family sacm_x --method sacm_x --variant "$PRESET" --seed "$SEED" \
+  --source-train <legacy-train-root> \
+  --source-eval  <legacy-eval-root> \
+  --out-root results/runs
 ```
 
-The index contains `family, method, seed, checkpoint, best_epoch, eval_root,
-metrics_csv, macro_csv, manifest`, so different seeds are separate rows.
+For baselines use `--family baseline --method <id> --variant default` and the
+legacy seed directory as both source roots.
